What is the purpose of LangChain?

LangChain is an open-source framework used to build LLM (Large Language Model) applications. It helps developers connect language models (such as GPT, Gemini, Groq, Claude, or Llama) with external tools, data sources, memory, and workflows to create intelligent AI applications.

Main Purpose of LangChain

The purpose of LangChain is to make it easy to build AI applications that can:

Connect to LLMs (OpenAI, Groq, Gemini, Anthropic, etc.)
Retrieve information from PDFs, databases, websites, and documents
Remember previous conversations (memory)
Use external tools and APIs
Build RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) systems
Create AI agents that can make decisions and perform tasks
Chain multiple AI steps together into a workflow

Why do we use LangChain?

Without LangChain:

User → LLM → Response

The model only answers based on its training data.

With LangChain:

User
   │
   ▼
LangChain
   ├── LLM
   ├── PDF
   ├── Database
   ├── Vector Database
   ├── Memory
   ├── APIs
   └── Tools
   │
   ▼
Final Answer

LangChain acts as the orchestrator, coordinating the interaction between the language model and other components.

Key Features

| Feature          | Purpose                                                  |
| ---------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |
| LLM Integration  | Connects to GPT, Gemini, Groq, Claude, etc.              |
| Prompt Templates | Creates reusable prompts                                 |
| Memory           | Remembers previous conversations                         |
| Chains           | Combines multiple AI steps into one workflow             |
| Agents           | Lets AI choose tools and actions automatically           |
| Tools            | Connects to search, calculators, APIs, databases, etc.   |
| Document Loaders | Reads PDFs, Word, CSV, websites, and more                |
| Text Splitters   | Breaks large documents into smaller chunks               |
| Embeddings       | Converts text into vectors for semantic search           |
| Vector Databases | Stores embeddings in FAISS, Chroma, Pinecone, etc.       |
| RAG              | Retrieves relevant information before generating answers |


